 247: /// This class is pure keymap logic: it does not mutate the controller, touch the
 248: /// clipboard, or know about widget state beyond the flags passed into [resolve].
 249: ///
 250: /// Shortcut configuration must preserve this boundary: configuration can add,
 251: /// override, disable, or pass through key combinations, but final execution
 252: /// still happens through the returned [EditorShortcutResolution]. When a future
 253: /// configuration object is supplied, it should keep the built-in keymap as the
 254: /// default layer and apply caller overrides only during resolution.
